<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Schnakenberg within-feather Turing wavelength of Anas platyrhynchos at 378.4 µm (Pass 2) (Anas platyrhynchos (Holocene, 0 Ma))",
        "Schnakenberg within-feather Turing wavelength of Anas platyrhynchos at 378.4 µm (Pass 2) faithfully reproduces Anas platyrhynchos (Holocene, 0 Ma) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Anas platyrhynchos (Holocene, 0 Ma) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Anas platyrhynchos (Holocene, 0 Ma)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A published mallard measurement of 378.4 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: Pixel identity between the GIF and the photograph. The fitness score is the orientation, radial-FFT, and coherency similarity.",
        "does_not_claim: That speculum hue or the green head is produced by this wavenumber.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Deviation PDE, Du scaled so lambda_star matches 0.0003784 m, axial bias for bars, q = 0.55 for ocelli.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: GIF display zoom. The portrait is coarser than 378 µm per pixel; the inset is a magnified vane, not a micrometre overlay.",
        "reported_in_source: Haupaix et al. 2018 somite prepattern is a longer-scale body stripe, not this 378 µm law.",
        "reported_in_source: Inaba & Chuong 2020 macro versus micro pigment levels.",
        "reported_in_source: Murray 1981: coat pre-pattern scale is set by diffusion, so a longer domain is a different wavelength.",
        "reported_in_source: Prum & Williamson 2002 within-feather reaction-diffusion classes.",
        "reported_in_source: Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics.",
        "reported_in_source: Stavenga et al. 2017 speculum colour is structural.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 wavenumber and diffusion-driven instability.",
        "transfer_boundary: Chronoseries 1/1 at 0 Ma. No predecessor or successor chronospecies. The 2.4 cm sibling is 62 detail wavelengths plus 79.2 µm." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Anas platyrhynchos" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Stripes, Spots & Ocelli" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Turing Wavenumber k_c" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Aves (Ornithes)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Anas" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength-s0.py; output: docs/media/anas_platyrhynchos_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Anas platyrhynchos (Holocene, 0 Ma); environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Turing 1952 wavenumber and diffusion-driven instability. | Schnakenberg 1979 two-species kinetics. | Murray 1981: coat pre-pattern scale is set by diffusion, so a longer domain is a different wavelength. | Prum & Williamson 2002 within-feather reaction-diffusion classes. | Inaba & Chuong 2020 macro versus micro pigment levels. | Haupaix et al. 2018 somite prepattern is a longer-scale body stripe, not this 378 µm law. | Stavenga et al. 2017 speculum colour is structural.; reconstructed_in_script: Deviation PDE, Du scaled so lambda_star matches 0.0003784 m, axial bias for bars, q = 0.55 for ocelli. | GIF display zoom. The portrait is coarser than 378 µm per pixel; the inset is a magnified vane, not a micrometre overlay.; transfer_boundary: Chronoseries 1/1 at 0 Ma. No predecessor or successor chronospecies. The 2.4 cm sibling is 62 detail wavelengths plus 79.2 µm.; does_not_claim: A published mallard measurement of 378.4 µm. | That speculum hue or the green head is produced by this wavenumber. | Pixel identity between the GIF and the photograph. The fitness score is the orientation, radial-FFT, and coherency similarity.]; phenomenon_size: 348 µm (0.0003476 m, log10=-3.459 m, tier=5_primordium_100um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 348 µm to 1.06 m): 348 µm:anas-platyrhynchos-bioelectric-polarity, 1.3 mm:anas-platyrhynchos-vertex-packing, 2.4 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-turing-wavelength, 4.4 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-clock-wavefront, 7.1 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-morphogen-condensation, 10.4 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-elastic-buckling, 17.6 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-flux-canalization, 23.3 cm:anas-platyrhynchos-branching-tree" ;
